[
  {
    "sha": "c6abeba7cc070619d5861dcf6170a4d7b458024a",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOQ_Wbs9oAKGM2YWJlYmE3Y2MwNzA2MTlkNTg2MWRjZjYxNzBhNGQ3YjQ1ODAyNGE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "ishaan-arora-1",
        "email": "ishaana612@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-01-30T18:58:20Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "ishaan-arora-1",
        "email": "ishaana612@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-01-30T18:58:20Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(vector): correct AVL comparison operator in vsetvl and vsetivli\n\nFix the first AVL comparison from `<` to `<=` to match the Sail\nreference model behavior.\n\nThe Sail model uses `AVL <= VLMAX` for the first comparison:\n```sail\nvl = if AVL <= VLMAX then to_bits(sizeof(xlen), AVL)\n     else if AVL < 2 * VLMAX then ...\n```\n\nBut the IDL was incorrectly using `<`:\n- vsetvl.yaml: `if (avl < vlmax)` -> `if (avl <= vlmax)`\n- vsetivli.yaml: `if (AVL < vlmax)` -> `if (AVL <= vlmax)`\n\nThis bug meant that when AVL exactly equals VLMAX, the code would\nincorrectly enter the `AVL < 2*VLMAX` branch instead of setting\nvl = AVL directly.\n\nAlso adds consistent spacing around `*` operator.",
